"help.body" = "Choose a topic in the flat sidebar. Numbered steps at the top move through explanations and practice. Completed steps carry a checkmark; the book icon identifies an explanation.\n\nThe SQL workspace appears for coding exercises. Press ⌘/ in the editor to toggle line comments. Outside text editing, use ← and → to move through steps, including the next topic. SQL runs automatically after a short pause in typing. Each execution uses a fresh isolated dataset. You can also run manually with ⌘Return. Live execution never completes an exercise: use Submit Answer (⇧⌘Return) for grading.\n\nOpen Schema to inspect tables and constraints. Select Preview to see sample rows. SQL NULL is shown explicitly. Select result rows and press ⌘C to copy them.\n\nUse one hint at a time. Reveal the worked solution only when you need it. Return to difficult exercises and try them again without the solution. Use submission history in the Learning Center to revisit mistakes.\n\nChange English or Russian in Settings. SQL keywords, table names, and executable code stay unchanged. All installed lessons, grading, hints, and progress work offline.\n\nYour progress is stored locally. File → Export Learning Progress creates a backup. Import merges completion and preserves existing drafts.";
